.TH FMT_ESCAPECHARJSON 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
fmt_escapecharjson \- Escape a character for JSON

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/fmt.h>

.IB size_t
.IB fmt_escapecharjson(char* dest, int c, int quote);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBfmt_escapecharjson\fR function escapes a character for JSON. It takes a destination buffer, a character, and a quote type as arguments. The function escapes the character if it is special in JSON, otherwise it copies the character unchanged.

The function takes the following parameters:
.IB char*
A pointer to the destination buffer.
.IB int
The character to escape.
.IB int
The type of quote to use.

The function returns the number of bytes written to the destination buffer.

The \fBfmt_escapecharjson\fR function is intended to be used to escape special characters for JSON, such as `\"`, `\\`, and `\b`.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBfmt_escapecharjson\fR function to escape a character for JSON:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/fmt.h>

int main() {
    char dest[20];
    int c = '"';

    size_t written = fmt_escapecharjson(dest, c, '"');

    printf("Written %d bytes: %s\n", written, dest);

    return 0;
}
.nef